WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 7.7 · Brand, Identity & Image
Credibility and trust signals

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
With no track record yet, the trust signals you can show matter even more.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.763
Trust signals are the visible signs that you are legitimate, accountable and effective. People look for them before they take part, buy or support you, and with no track record yet they matter even more.

4
00:00:28.163 --> 00:00:28.763
From claim to signal

5
00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:40.833
Who you are: Legal status, or an honest note that you are registering, and named founders. For example: “Registering as a company with a social purpose”, with both founders named on the website.

6
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:49.941
Published policies: Safeguarding, privacy and complaints policies, easy to find. For example: A one-page safeguarding summary and a named contact for trainees and families.

7
00:00:49.941 --> 00:01:00.530
Evidence: Results with their method and date, or what you will measure. For example: “First results due after the pilot: how many trainees finished and found work.”

8
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:11.207
Permissions: Partners, testimonials and endorsements shown only with written permission. For example: The youth centre’s name appears only after its manager agreed in writing.

9
00:01:11.607 --> 00:01:12.207
Why it matters

10
00:01:12.207 --> 00:01:17.881
1. People check you before they take part, buy, join or support.

11
00:01:17.881 --> 00:01:23.556
2. Those who carry the most risk look hardest at the signals.

12
00:01:23.556 --> 00:01:30.230
3. One misleading claim can undo credibility before you have built it.

13
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.230
Where they appear

14
00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:35.793
1. Your website, social profiles, proposals and printed materials.

15
00:01:35.793 --> 00:01:41.837
2. Your plan to close the gaps that matter most to key audiences.

16
00:01:41.837 --> 00:01:47.030
3. Your safeguarding and complaints policies, made visible.

17
00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.030
What to avoid

18
00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:52.222
Overstating a partnership, endorsement, status or result.

19
00:01:52.222 --> 00:01:57.526
Hiding who the founders are or how decisions are made.

20
00:01:57.526 --> 00:02:03.089
Vague claims like “huge impact” with no evidence.

21
00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.489
You audit your trust signals and plan the gaps to close.

22
00:02:05.489 --> 00:02:09.489
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:10.989 --> 00:02:14.089
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
